const html = "<h1 class=\"legal-title\" id=\"ckT\">Cookie Policy</h1><p class=\"upd\">Last updated: 19 November 2026</p>\n  <p>Olexweb uses no advertising cookies. We use analytics cookies only if you say yes in the cookie bar.</p>\n  <h2>Analytics cookies (only with your yes)</h2><p>If you accept, Google Analytics sets cookies (named <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_…</code>, kept for up to 2 years) to count visits and see which pages help people, so we can improve the site. Your IP address is shortened and nothing is used for ads. If you choose “No thanks”, Google Analytics never loads. <a href=\"/cookies#settings\">Change your choice</a> at any time.</p>\n  <h2>Anonymous visit counts</h2><p>We also count visits anonymously without cookies: a random number kept only while the tab is open, never linked to you, and switched off if your browser asks not to be tracked.</p>\n  <h2>What the site stores on your device (no cookies)</h2>\n  <ul><li><strong>Your cookie choice.</strong> So the bar isn’t shown again.</li><li><strong>Sound preference.</strong> If you turn the anthem off, your browser remembers it.</li><li><strong>Liked and saved articles.</strong> So the buttons show your choice and your saved articles appear in the Blog’s Saved tab. The site counts likes and saves only as anonymous totals.</li><li><strong>The chat.</strong> Whether you closed the chat box.</li><li><strong>Opening seen.</strong> For the current visit only, that you have already seen the opening animation.</li></ul>\n  <p>These stay in your browser and are not used to track you.</p>\n  <h2>Other services</h2><p>The site’s typefaces load from Google Fonts. The Privacy Policy explains exactly what is counted.</p>\n  <h2>Clearing it</h2><p>You can clear cookies and site data at any time in your browser’s settings.</p>\n  <h2>Contact</h2><p><a href=\"mailto:info@olexweb.com\">info@olexweb.com</a></p>";
